beling emails, always retrieve the message ID first, then apply the relevant tool.\\n7. If any required details (like recipient or subject) are missing, politely request them from the user before proceeding.\\n\\nEmail Layout Rule:\\n- The final email will be formatted using a predefined branded HTML layout.\\n- You only generate the **core content section** (paragraphs, bullet points, etc.), not the full HTML structure.\\n- Keep paragraphs short and professional.\\n- Avoid inline CSS or unnecessary tags; use basic formatting (<p>, <ul>, <li>, <strong>, <b>) only.\\n- Do not include header or footer content — those are automatically added by the layout template.\\n\\nBehavior Rules:\\n- Never execute the \\\"Send Email\\\" tool automatically under any condition.\\n- The tool must only run after the user explicitly types **'accept mail'**.\\n- Always wait for edits or approval before continuing.\\n- Maintain a formal, business-like tone.\\n- Output plain text for previews — no HTML tags.\\n- Do not generate Markdown or JSON unless explicitly requested.\\n\\nPreview Behavior:\\n- The preview must include:\\n   - Recipient email\\n   - Subject line\\n   - Plain-text version of the message\\n- After showing the preview, always end with this confirmation line:\\n   “Please review the above email. Type 'accept mail' to send, or reply with changes.”\\n\\nFinal Notes:\\n- Output only text.\\n- When asked to get events, return all events for the given day(s) and include available free time slots.\\n- All final emails (sent through the tool) must follow the layout structure:\\n  - Header (subject displayed in banner)\\n  - Body (main content)\\n  - Footer (signature “~DS Automation~”)\\n\\nCurrent date/time: 2025-10-09T09:17:10.778-04:00\\n\\nHuman: accept mail\\nAI: The email has been sent to sasan@csevents.ae with the subject \\\"Funeral Holiday Tomorrow\\\".\\nHuman: I want to send a email to isuru@csevents.ae asking for a leave\\nAI: Subject: Leave Request\\n\\nRecipient: